    "processes": ["sound-change"],
    "headline": "Tōtoi is from Old Japanese, first attested in the Kojiki of 712 CE, and is possibly derived from 太い (futoi, “fat”).",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "⟨taputo₁ki⟩ → */taɸutokʲi/ → /toːtoi/"
      },
      {
        "quote": "From Old Japanese. First attested in the Kojiki of 712 CE. From Early Middle Japanese adjective 尊(とうと)し (tōtoshi), with the 終(しゅう)止(し)形(けい) (shūshikei, “predicative form”) ending in し (shi) first replaced with the 連(れん)体(たい)形(けい) (rentaikei, “attributive form”) ending in き (ki), and then with the medial /-k-/ falling out to result in an ending of い (i)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Possibly derived from 太い (futoi, “fat”)."
      }
    ],
    "wiktionaryDump": "2026-09-02"
  },
