    "date": "2026-04-13",
    "term": "惑星",
    "kana": "わくせい",
    "meaning": "planet",
    "level": "N1",
    "pos": ["noun (common) (futsuumeishi)"],
    "priority": ["news1", "nf13"],
    "stratum": "kango",
    "processes": ["compound", "wasei"],
    "headline": "Wakusei is a calque of Dutch dwaalster (“wander star”), 惑 (waku, “to move about confusedly, to wander”) plus 星 (sei, “star”), coined in 1792 by Motoki Yoshinaga.",
    "morphemes": [
      {
        "text": "惑",
        "reading": "わく",
        "meaning": "to move about confusedly, to wander"
      },
      {
        "text": "星",
        "reading": "せい",
        "meaning": "star"
      }
    ],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "Wasei kango: Calque of Dutch dwaalster (literally “wander star”), composed as a compound of 惑 (waku, “to move about confusedly, to wander”) + 星 (sei, “star”). Probably related to 熒惑 (MC hweng hwok)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Coined in 1792 by Dutch-Japanese translator Motoki Yoshinaga in his 太陽窮理了解説 (Taiyō Kyūri Ryōkai Setsu, “Theory of Understanding on the Natural Study of the Sun”), a translation of Copernicus's De revolutionibus orbium coelestium and its heliocentric model."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Also cited in the 1805 work 和蘭通舶 (Oranda Tsūhaku, “Holland Liner”) by Shiba Kōkan."
      }
    ],
    "examples": [
